# FDD 25 review — "25 - Educator Preparation Providers - User" (Features 25.1-25.4),
# ingested per abox/mied-v3/fdd-review/CONVENTIONS.md against the mied-v3 EPP graph
# (epp-domain.ttl / epp-permissions.ttl / epp-api.ttl / epp-sequences.ttl, all loaded
# together — EPP has no *-technical-design.ttl in this batch, so none is referenced).
#
# Source: two docx, read together as one logical FDD 25 (the folder's own convention,
# same pattern CONVENTIONS.md documents for FDD 16/11 and FDD 17):
# - "25.1, 25.3 - Worklist and Recommendation.docx" — Feature 25.1 (worklist search) and
#   25.3 (Hold/Deny/Cancel/Recommend actions, both the standard credential worklist and
#   the Approval worklist).
# - "25.2, 25.4 - EPP - Candidate Tracking.docx" — Feature 25.2 (Candidate Tracking:
#   Pending Verification / Verified Candidates worklists, accept/reject, status update,
#   program management) and 25.4 (bulk candidate-tracking file upload).
# Both read via their .md sibling first, then unzipped for word/comments.xml,
# commentsExtended.xml (thread structure), and word/media wireframes. The "HIGH LEVEL
# SCENARIOS" paraphrase tables in both docs (25 rows in the Worklist doc, 34 in the
# Candidate Tracking doc) restate the same content as the Addendum's numbered stories at
# coarser grain and are skipped per CONVENTIONS.md — every item in both HLS tables traces
# to one of the 11 Addendum stories modeled below; nothing in either HLS table describes
# behavior absent from the Addendum.
#
# Requirement unit: the Addendum's own numbering — 25.1.1-25.1.2, 25.3.1-25.3.2 (Worklist
# doc); 25.2.1-25.2.6, 25.4.1 (Candidate Tracking doc). 11 stories total, all in genuine
# "As a <role>, I want <goal>, so that <benefit>" form — modeled as sd:UserStory
# throughout, no bare NFR or non-narrative item found in either Addendum.
#
# THIS FDD IS UNUSUALLY WELL PRE-COVERED: unlike several other FDD passes in this batch,
# epp-domain.ttl/epp-sequences.ttl/epp-api.ttl were themselves converted directly from
# epp-domain.md/epp-sequences.md/epp-api.yml, which already describe almost exactly the
# same worklist-search / hold-deny-cancel-recommend / candidate-tracking / bulk-upload
# functionality this FDD's Addendum spells out narratively. As a result this pass reads
# largely as CONFIRMATORY (matching credentialing's own precedent for FDD 09 against an
# already-FDD-aware profpractice-domain.ttl) rather than exploratory — 9 of 11 stories are
# fully or near-fully satisfied by nodes already in the v3 graph, with only small,
# genuinely new gaps surfacing (an unmodeled "download search results as Word/Excel/PDF"
# export, an unmodeled cross-domain "Educator Profile" composite page, and one narrower
# "bulk Add Program across multiple candidates" operation gap alongside the already-bulk
# "Status Update" operation).
#
# RESOLVES FDD 29's OPEN GAPS.md ITEM ("Candidate Tracking and Recommendation (25)... FDD
# 25 itself wasn't reviewed as part of this pass, so it's unconfirmed whether
# epp:Seq_BulkUploadCandidateTrackingData actually covers what FDD 29's Dependencies
# section is pointing at"): CONFIRMED, with minor caveats. Feature 25.4.1 ("As an EPP User
# or MiEdWorkforce System Admin user, I want to upload a bulk file for reporting teacher
# candidate tracking...") describes exactly the CSV-upload / Unique-ID-validation /
# program-approval-validation / partial-success / downloadable-error-report shape that
# epp:Seq_BulkUploadCandidateTrackingData (and its epp:Op_InitiateBulkUpload /
# epp:Op_CompleteBulkUpload / epp:Op_BulkCreateEnrollments / epp:BulkUploadCompletedEvent
# backing) already models end-to-end, right down to the "reject records where the student
# has not yet established a MiEdWorkforce account/Unique ID" validation step matching the
# sequence's own "Validate Unique IDs exist in IAM" / "Skip row, include in error report"
# error scenario. Two caveats, neither large enough to justify a fresh coverage-gap
# Annotation on their own: (1) 25.4.1's own requirement that the audit log "distinguish
# actions taken by an admin on behalf of an EPP and the EPP user" is finer-grained than
# the sequence's generic "Capture audit trail with bulk upload job ID" — the uploader's
# identity is captured (uploadedBy in the initiate payload) but the admin-vs-EPP-user
# distinction isn't called out as its own field anywhere; (2) HLS Use Case 34 ("System
# Admin downloads and extracts the submitted data") has no dedicated modeled operation,
# but is a plausible fit for the already-generic docs:Op_DownloadDocument against the
# staging container — not a hard gap. See epp:Req_25_4_1's own sd:notes.
#
# Comments (21 in the Worklist doc, 30 in the Candidate Tracking doc, read via
# comments.xml + commentsExtended.xml): almost all are resolved clarification threads
# (terminology definitions — "what is Approval Type/Category", "define duplicate" — and
# UI corrections already folded into the final Addendum text) with no live contradiction
# on the scale of FDD 29's cover-letter thread. One thread surfaced a genuine, still-live
# finding, modeled below as Question_MissingCertEndorsementProviderStories: a reviewer
# asks "Where does 'Certifications & Endorsements' and 'Provider Details & Contacts' user
# stories will be?" and is told "Missing user stories" / "Working on getting wireframes
# for this so that the user stories can be revised" — i.e. the FDD's own landing-page
# wireframe (see below) shows navigation cards for these two areas that were never
# written up as numbered stories anywhere in either document. Tracked changes: doc1 has
# none; doc2 has 25 w:ins/12 w:del spans, not reconstructed as a diff per CONVENTIONS.md
# (nothing found in a manual scan that isn't already reflected in the final Addendum text
# or the comment-thread corrections already folded into sd:notes below).
#
# Wireframes: doc1 has 13 images (5 numbered "Wireframe N" captions covering 6 embeds —
# Wireframe 1 appears twice, "Option 1"/"Option 2" — plus 7 further uncaptioned
# higher-fidelity "Addendum" screenshots); doc2 has 20 images (10 numbered "Wireframe N"
# captions, 1:1 with embeds 1-10, plus 10 further uncaptioned Addendum screenshots).
# Captions in both documents immediately FOLLOW their image (confirmed by checking
# embed/caption byte-offsets in document.xml directly, not assumed) — same order FDD
# 29's own pass found, opposite of FDD 11/16's caption-before-image pattern; a reminder
# this is genuinely per-document and worth re-checking each time, not a fixed rule.
# Of 33 total images, 12 were individually viewed and extracted (listed below); the
# remainder were sampled across both documents' span (early/mid/late in the Addendum
# sections) and confirmed to be further screens of the same worklist/candidate-tracking/
# application-review flows already covered by the ones extracted, not a distinct
# undocumented feature area, per CONVENTIONS.md's depth-calibration guidance for
# near-duplicate image sets.

@prefix sd:    <urn:solutiondesign:ontology:> .
@prefix oa:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/oa#> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix epp:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:epp:> .
@prefix docs:  <urn:solutiondesign:instance:documents:> .
@prefix rpt:   <urn:solutiondesign:instance:reporting:> .

#################################################################
# Source documents
#################################################################

epp:Fdd25WorklistDoc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "fdd" ;
    sd:section "functional-design-docs/25 - Educator Preparation Providers - User/25.1, 25.3 - Worklist and Recommendation.docx" ;
    sd:notes "Covers Features 25.1 (worklist search) and 25.3 (Hold/Deny/Cancel/Recommend actions). Authors Vidhya Punniyamoorthy and Beth Dontje (DTMB); approved by Beth Dontje (MDE) and Caitlin Groom (CEPI), both 08/05/2025 per the signoff table — but comments.xml carries dated entries through 2026-03-10, after that nominal approval date, the same 'still revised after signoff' pattern FDD 29's own review noted for its document." .

epp:Fdd25CandidateTrackingDoc a sd:SourceDocument ;
    sd:docType "fdd" ;
    sd:section "functional-design-docs/25 - Educator Preparation Providers - User/25.2, 25.4 - EPP - Candidate Tracking.docx" ;
    sd:notes "Covers Features 25.2 (Candidate Tracking worklist) and 25.4 (bulk file upload). Authors Vidhya Punniyamoorthy, Beth Dontje, and Caitlin Groom (DTMB); same approvers/signoff date as Fdd25WorklistDoc. comments.xml carries dated entries through 2026-04-03." .

