#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 25.1: EPP workflow search (worklist)
#################################################################

epp:Req_25_1_1 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "25.1.1" ;
    sd:title "Search and filter the EPP credential application worklist" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce user with Education Preparation Provider (EPP) permissions, I want to search and filter the worklist of credential applications, so that I can locate specific applications or groups of applications requiring my review." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Navigate to the worklist via hamburger menu > Certificate Applications; freeform search bar (default text 'Type to search'); results table sorted ascending by Submitted Date with columns Application Number (hyperlink), First/Last Name, Student ID, Unique ID, Certificate Type, Has Conviction? (red font if Yes), Status, Submitted Date, Last Modified By, Summary (hyperlink, opens read-only); dropdown filters per the main Business Specifications list (Certificate Type, Status, Application #, First/Last Name, SSN, Unique ID, Student ID, Uses Alternative Pass? for Teacher only, plus Approval Category/Type for the Approval tab); Clear button restores defaults; 'No results found' messaging." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:Op_SearchApplicationReviews, epp:Op_SearchApprovalApplicationReviews, epp:Perm_ApplicationsView, epp:Perm_ApprovalsView, epp:Rule_ConvictionFlagManualReview, epp:Seq_SearchCredentialApplicationsForReview ;
    sd:notes "Direct match: Op_SearchApplicationReviews's own ApplicationReviewSummary projection explicitly carries hasConviction/usesAlternativePass flags for exactly this red-font/Teacher-only-filter behavior. The Approval tab's own Approval Category/Type filter values (Teacher, Administrator, Other, Educated out-of-state Special Education Admin, Educated out-of-state School Social Worker, Permit) match epp:ApprovalCategory's description almost verbatim. Wireframe25_Worklist1 (confirmed by viewing) directly corroborates the tabbed worklist layout." ;
    sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25WorklistDoc .

epp:Req_25_1_2 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "25.1.2" ;
    sd:title "Navigate from the worklist to application detail and the Educator Profile" ;
    sd:statement "As an EPP user reviewing a specific application, I need hyperlinks on the Application Number, so that I can view the detailed application status screen and the comprehensive Educator Profile page." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Clicking an Application Number opens the detailed review screen; the Applicant Name on that screen is a hyperlink to the Educator Profile page (current and historical demographic info); the review screen has a Details tab (Personal Information, Application Information, MTTC Information: Endorsement Name/Test Code/Has Passed?/Date Passed/Exam Date), an Internal Remarks tab (Comment/Created By/Date Created), and an Audit Log tab (User ID, date/time of status change, Previous Status, New Status)." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:Op_GetApplicationReview, epp:Op_GetInternalRemarks, epp:Op_AddInternalRemark, epp:Op_GetRemarksHistory, epp:Seq_ViewCredentialApplicationDetailForReview ;
    sd:notes "Direct match for the Details/Internal Remarks/Audit Log tab structure (epp-sequences.ttl's own sequence names these tabs 'Details / MTTC Information / Internal Remarks / Audit Log' almost verbatim, and Op_GetRemarksHistory's projection is exactly the action/actionBy/actionAt shape the Audit Log tab needs). Wireframe25_AddendumApplicationReviewDetail (confirmed by viewing) directly corroborates this. The 'Educator Profile page' destination itself, however, is NOT modeled anywhere in this graph as a first-class thing — see Question_EducatorProfilePageNotModeled below (this is the first FDD 25 story to reference it, but not the first FDD in the batch to reference an 'Educator Profile' screen at all; FDD 17's own school-admin wireframe search flow references the same destination by name)." ;
    sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25WorklistDoc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "The 'Educator Profile' page — a composite, multi-domain screen with Demographic Information/Credentials/Employment/Professional Development/Education tabs, confirmed by viewing Wireframe25_AddendumEducatorProfileEducatorTab — is referenced by name repeatedly across this FDD (25.1.2's Applicant Name hyperlink; the Approval-tab worklist's own Name hyperlink; the Candidate Tracking worklist's First Name hyperlink in 25.2.5) and, per FDD 17's own school-admin wireframe, at least one other already-reviewed FDD. No aggregate, ApiOperation, or Sequence anywhere in the mied-v3 graph models this page as a first-class thing — each tab's underlying data IS separately modeled (iam:Op_GetUser for demographics, cred:Op_GetEducatorCredentials for Credentials, presumably proflearning/profpractice feed the Professional Development/other tabs, epp itself feeds the Education tab), but nothing represents the composite profile page/navigation shell itself. Likely belongs to a cross-cutting capability (Dashboards, or a dedicated 'Educator Profile' feature) rather than any single domain — flagged here rather than forced onto EPP specifically, and worth a GAPS.md entry given it now recurs across two independently-reviewed FDDs (17 and 25)." ;
    oa:hasTarget epp:Req_25_1_2 ;
    sd:impact "M" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25WorklistDoc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "out-of-scope" ;
    rdfs:comment "Comment thread 19/20/21 in the Worklist document (Punniyamoorthy: 'Where does \"Certifications & Endorsements\" and \"Provider Details & Contacts\" user stories will be?' / Dontje: 'Missing user stories' / Sinha: 'Working on getting wireframes for this so that the user stories can be revised') confirms the two rightmost navigation cards on the shared 'Education Prep' landing page (Wireframe25_AddendumEducationPrepLanding1/2, confirmed by viewing) were never written up as numbered stories in EITHER FDD 25 document — an acknowledged gap in the FDD's own paper trail, not something missed by this review. These two areas (EPP certificate-category/endorsement approvals, and EPP provider/contact details) are exactly epp:EducatorPreparationProviderAggregate's own territory and are already covered by FDD 13 ('EPP - Admin'), which epp-domain.ttl's own Open Question #11 note already cites and which is being reviewed concurrently by a separate pass in this same session — out-of-scope for FDD 25 specifically, not a gap in the EPP domain model as a whole (epp:Seq_ManageCertificateCategoryApprovals / epp:Seq_ManageApprovedEndorsements / epp:Seq_UpdateEPPConfiguration already cover this territory)." ;
    oa:hasTarget epp:EducatorPreparationProviderAggregate ;
    sd:impact "L" ; sd:status "resolved" ; sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25WorklistDoc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 25.3: Recommending Candidates
#################################################################

epp:Req_25_3_1 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "25.3.1" ;
    sd:title "Hold, Deny, Cancel, or Recommend a credential application under EPP review" ;
    sd:statement "As a MiEdWorkforce user with Education Preparation Provider (EPP) permissions, I want to perform specific actions (Hold, Deny, Cancel, or Recommend) on a candidate's detailed application screen, so that I can validate their endorsements against test scores and progress the application through the approval workflow." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Single-select Action dropdown (Select/Hold/Deny/Cancel/Recommend); Hold/Deny/Cancel collect Application Remarks (optional per this story's own text) and optional Internal Remarks, then set status accordingly; Recommend collects License Type and an endorsement table (Recommend checkbox, Endorsement Name, Code, Grade Band, Action by applicant, inline Edit/Delete, Add Endorsement), validates at least one endorsement is added/recommended, and on Submit routes in-state applicants to 'Pending Payment' or out-of-state applicants directly to the OEE/State Credential Admin worklist." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:Op_HoldApplication, epp:Op_DenyApplication, epp:Op_CancelApplication, epp:Op_RecommendApplication, epp:Seq_PlaceCredentialApplicationOnHold, epp:Seq_DenyCredentialApplication, epp:Seq_CancelCredentialApplicationReview, epp:Seq_RecommendCandidateForCredential, epp:Rule_EPPRecommendationTriggersPaymentOrOEEReview, epp:Rule_EPPRecommendationRequiresMTTCPass, epp:Rule_EPPProgramApprovalScope ;
    sd:notes "Excellent, near-exhaustive match: this story is essentially the narrative source epp-domain.md's Rule_EPPRecommendationTriggersPaymentOrOEEReview was itself built from (in-state -> Pending Payment / out-of-state -> OEE routing, worded almost identically). Wireframe25_Worklist3 (Recommend) and Wireframe25_Worklist4 (Deny) both confirmed by viewing. One genuine new detail: Wireframe25_Worklist4 shows a 'Send Email?' checkbox on the Deny action, matching this story's own 'Optional' framing for sending the Application Remarks email — the toggle itself isn't separately modeled anywhere (Communications owns the actual send mechanics), not raised as its own gap since it's a small UI/Communications-boundary detail, not an EPP-domain one." ;
    sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25WorklistDoc .

epp:Req_25_3_2 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "25.3.2" ;
    sd:title "Deny an Approval application and return it to the requesting ISD/School District" ;
    sd:statement "As an EPP User, I want to deny an Approval application that does not meet program requirements, so that the system automatically notifies the requesting ISD/School District and returns the application to their worklist for resolution." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Deny is a selectable Action option on Approval-tab applications; Remarks are required (submission blocked if blank); on submission, status updates to Deny, an email is sent to the originating ISD/School District, the application is removed from the EPP worklist and reassigned to the ISD/School District worklist, and the action (status change, remarks, Modified By, Action Date) is captured in the Approval Application History." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:Op_DenyApprovalApplication, epp:Seq_DenyApprovalApplication, epp:Rule_ApprovalApplicationDenialReturnsToISD ;
    sd:notes "Exact match, down to the required-remarks validation and the History-capture fields — epp:Seq_DenyApprovalApplication's own error scenario ('Missing required remarks > Validation error') and event flow ('EventBus--)CredService: Return application to ISD/School District', 'EventBus--)CommService: Trigger notification to ISD with denial remarks') mirror this story almost verbatim. This story is also, in effect, the narrative source for Rule_ApprovalApplicationDenialReturnsToISD." ;
    sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25WorklistDoc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 25.2: Track Candidates
#################################################################

epp:Req_25_2_1 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "25.2.1" ;
    sd:title "Switch between Pending Verification and Verified Candidates worklists" ;
    sd:statement "As an EPP user, I need to easily switch between Pending Verification and Verified Candidates lists on the Candidate Tracking worklist, so that I can efficiently manage candidates based on their enrollment status." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Navigate via Dashboard > Education Prep > Candidates; two tabs (Pending Verification, Verified Candidates); each tab has a freeform search bar, a results table (per-tab column set matching the Business Specifications section), the same filter set (Program Level, Program Type [Teacher/School Administrator only], First/Last Name, Student ID, Unique ID, plus Status and date ranges on the Verified tab), 'No results found' messaging, and the ability to download the worksheet as Word/Excel/PDF." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:Op_SearchCandidateEnrollments, epp:Seq_SearchPendingEnrollmentVerifications, epp:Seq_SearchEnrolledCandidates ;
    sd:notes "Search/filter/tab-switch behavior is a direct match (Wireframe25_CandTrack1 confirmed by viewing). The Word/Excel/PDF worksheet-download capability, however, has no counterpart anywhere in this graph: epp-api.ttl exposes only JSON list endpoints, documents-api.ttl has no table-export operation, and reporting-capability.ttl's own Rule_NotEveryDashboardIsAPowerBIReport explicitly argues this kind of simple UI-level table export should be a native in-domain component rather than a Reporting-capability concern — meaning it isn't Reporting's gap to fill either. See the coverage-gap Annotation below." ;
    sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25CandidateTrackingDoc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "25.2.1 requires the Pending Verification and Verified Candidates worklist tables to be downloadable in Word, Excel, and PDF formats. No export/download operation for a search-results table exists anywhere in epp-api.ttl, documents-api.ttl, or reporting-api.ttl — and reporting-capability.ttl's own Rule_NotEveryDashboardIsAPowerBIReport (Power BI embedding is for complex/cross-domain/scheduled-refresh reporting, not simple UI-level table exports) argues this specific capability was never meant to live in the Reporting bounded context either. A genuine, small, EPP-side gap: nothing in the converted domains currently supports it." ;
    oa:hasTarget epp:Req_25_2_1 ;
    sd:impact "L" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25CandidateTrackingDoc .

epp:Req_25_2_2 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "25.2.2" ;
    sd:title "Bulk Accept or Reject enrollment on multiple Pending Verification candidates" ;
    sd:statement "As an EPP user, I need to perform a bulk Accept or Reject Enrollment action on multiple candidates simultaneously from the Pending Verification list, to save time during verification." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Select one or multiple Pending Verification records; Accept Enrollment and Reject Enrollment options become available; Reject sets status to Rejected and sends a templated notification email; Accept prompts for Enrollment Start Date/Program Level/Program(s)/Program Type then sets status to Enrolled and sends a notification email; both actions capture audit details (Modified By, Modified Date)." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:Op_BulkAcceptEnrollments, epp:Op_BulkRejectEnrollments, epp:Seq_AcceptCandidateEnrollment, epp:Seq_RejectCandidateEnrollment, epp:CandidateEnrollmentVerifiedEvent, epp:CandidateEnrollmentRejectedEvent ;
    sd:notes "Direct, complete match — epp:Seq_AcceptCandidateEnrollment/Seq_RejectCandidateEnrollment already model exactly this bulk shape, including the notification-email trigger via comm:CommunicationsContext's subscription to both events." ;
    sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25CandidateTrackingDoc .

epp:Req_25_2_3 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "25.2.3" ;
    sd:title "Prevent duplicate enrollment records when accepting enrollment" ;
    sd:statement "As an EPP user, when accepting enrollment, the system must check for duplicate record creation upon saving, preventing accidental double entry." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "On Save during Accept Enrollment, validate for duplicates defined as same Student/Unique ID + same EPP + same Program Level + same Program Type; block creation and display a clear error message if a duplicate is detected." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:Seq_AcceptCandidateEnrollment ;
    sd:notes "Matches epp:Seq_AcceptCandidateEnrollment's own key decision ('Duplicate Check: Prevents duplicate enrollment records for same candidate/EPP/program') and error scenario. Comment thread 18/20/21 in the source document shows the exact duplicate definition (Same EPP + Student/Unique ID + Program Level + Program Type for enrollment-level duplicates, distinct from Same Program + Grade Band for the program-level duplicate check in Rule_DuplicateProgramPrevention) was clarified during review — both concepts are present in this domain's model, just under different rules; not itself a gap." ;
    sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25CandidateTrackingDoc .

epp:Req_25_2_4 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "25.2.4" ;
    sd:title "Bulk Add Program and Status Update on Verified Candidates" ;
    sd:statement "As an EPP user, I need the ability to Add Program and perform a Status Update (including Enrolled, Student Teaching, Placed, Exited) in bulk on the Verified Candidates list, to update large groups of candidates as they progress through the program." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Verified Candidates worklist offers View/Add Program/Status Update radio options (View default); selecting one or multiple records + Add Program lets the user choose Program + Grade Band from dropdowns with Edit/Confirm/Delete before saving, blocking duplicates (same EPP + Student/Unique ID + Program + Grade Band); selecting Status Update changes status for multiple candidates to the route-appropriate set (Traditional: Enrolled/Student Teaching/Post Student Teaching/Inactive/Rejected/Exited; Alt Route: Enrolled/Placed/Inactive/Rejected/Exited), validates at least one program exists when moving to a placement status, and requires Exit Reason/Date on Exited or Program Detail/Enrollment Start Date on Rejected-to-Enrolled." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:Op_BulkUpdateCandidateStatus, epp:Seq_UpdateCandidateEnrollmentStatus, epp:Rule_EnrollmentStatusStateMachine, epp:Rule_CandidateProgramAssignmentRequiredForPlacement, epp:Rule_DuplicateProgramPrevention ;
    sd:notes "Status Update half is a direct, complete match (epp:Op_BulkUpdateCandidateStatus's own projection already conditionally requires exitDate/exitReason or enrollmentDate/programLevel/programType exactly as this story describes). The Add Program half is only PARTIALLY satisfied: epp-api.ttl's program-management operations (epp:Op_AddCandidateProgram et al.) all operate on a single enrollmentId — there is no bulk-add-program-to-multiple-candidates counterpart to Op_BulkUpdateCandidateStatus's bulk-status pattern. Wireframe25_CandTrack9 (confirmed by viewing) independently corroborates the route-restricted status set. See the coverage-gap Annotation below." ;
    sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25CandidateTrackingDoc .

[] a sd:Annotation ; oa:motivatedBy oa:reviewing ; sd:findingType "coverage-gap" ;
    rdfs:comment "25.2.4 describes 'Add Program' as a bulk action applicable to one or multiple selected Verified Candidates in a single operation, parallel to the already-bulk Status Update action (epp:Op_BulkUpdateCandidateStatus). No bulk-add-program operation exists in epp-api.ttl — epp:Op_AddCandidateProgram/Op_UpdateCandidateProgram/Op_DeleteCandidateProgram (used by epp:Seq_ManageCandidatePrograms) all operate on one enrollmentId at a time. A narrower, lower-impact analogue of the same 'bulk vs. single' asymmetry the ontology already tolerates elsewhere (e.g. Reject Enrollment has no per-candidate remarks requirement unlike single-application denial) — worth a small addition (a bulk variant of Op_AddCandidateProgram) rather than a redesign." ;
    oa:hasTarget epp:Req_25_2_4 ;
    sd:impact "L" ; sd:status "open" ; sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25CandidateTrackingDoc .

epp:Req_25_2_5 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "25.2.5" ;
    sd:title "View and edit a Verified Candidate's detailed enrollment and program record" ;
    sd:statement "As an EPP User, I want to see a detailed view of a Verified Candidate, so that I can review their current enrollment status, program history, and toggle between viewing internal enrollment data and enrollment data from other providers." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Clicking a candidate's name opens the individual profile on the Education tab (Enrolled Date, Program Level, EPP Provider, Status, Exit Date/Reason); an Edit modal allows changing Enrollment Date/Program Level/EPP Provider/Status (with Exit Date/Reason required for Exited, and Program Detail/Enrollment Start Date required for Rejected-to-Enrolled, plus the same at-least-one-program validation for placement statuses); a Program(s) table (Program Name/Type/Grade Band/Modified By/Modified Date) supports add/edit/delete via a modal." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:Seq_ViewCandidateEnrollmentDetail, epp:Op_GetCandidateEnrollment, epp:Op_UpdateCandidateStatus, epp:Seq_ManageCandidatePrograms, epp:Op_AddCandidateProgram, epp:Op_UpdateCandidateProgram, epp:Op_DeleteCandidateProgram, epp:Seq_ViewCrossEPPEnrollmentHistory ;
    sd:notes "Direct, complete match across both the detail-view and edit-modal halves of this story; Op_UpdateCandidateStatus's own projection (conditional exitDate/exitReason or enrollmentDate/programLevel/programType fields) matches this story's edit-modal validation exactly. Wireframe25_AddendumEducatorProfileEducationTab and Wireframe25_CandTrack10 (both confirmed by viewing) directly corroborate the Education tab layout and the cross-EPP toggle respectively." ;
    sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25CandidateTrackingDoc .

epp:Req_25_2_6 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "25.2.6" ;
    sd:title "View and act on an individual Pending Verification candidate" ;
    sd:statement "As an EPP User, I want to see a detailed view of a Pending Verification Candidate, so that I can review their current enrollment status to either Accept or Reject their Enrollment." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Clicking a Pending Verification candidate opens their profile with an 'Unverified Enrollment' alert; displays Program Type and a single-select action dropdown (Accept Enrollment / Reject Enrollment); Accept collects Enrollment Start Date + Program Level/Type (with duplicate check), sets status to Enrolled, and emails the candidate; Reject sets status to Rejected and emails the candidate; both save audit details; the screen also supports adding/editing/deleting programs (same duplicate rule as elsewhere: same Program + Grade Band)." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:Op_BulkAcceptEnrollments, epp:Op_BulkRejectEnrollments, epp:Seq_AcceptCandidateEnrollment, epp:Seq_RejectCandidateEnrollment, epp:Op_AddCandidateProgram ;
    sd:notes "Functionally this is the same accept/reject/program-management behavior as Req_25_2_2/25_2_4, exercised at the individual-candidate level rather than from a bulk-selected list — the existing bulk operations (accepting/rejecting an array of one candidateId) already cover this cleanly; no dedicated single-candidate accept/reject endpoint is needed and none is modeled separately. Wireframe25_AddendumAcceptEnrollmentReview (confirmed by viewing) directly corroborates this individual-level screen, including the editable Program(s) table alongside the Accept/Reject dropdown." ;
    sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25CandidateTrackingDoc .

#################################################################
# Requirements — Feature 25.4: Document upload
#################################################################

epp:Req_25_4_1 a sd:UserStory ;
    sd:requirementId "25.4.1" ;
    sd:title "Bulk-upload a file for reporting/updating candidate tracking data" ;
    sd:statement "As an EPP User or MiEdWorkforce System Admin user, I want to upload a bulk file for reporting teacher candidate tracking, so that I can efficiently enroll multiple verified candidates into my program and update their statuses without manual entry for each individual." ;
    sd:acceptanceCriteria "Navigate Dashboard > Education Prep > Candidates, click Add Student dropdown > Upload; the system accepts files only matching the defined type/size/template; processes rows by the student's Unique ID, rejecting rows for students without an established MiEdWorkforce account/Unique ID; if the file includes Program Type/Level, validates the EPP is approved to offer those specific programs and errors on unapproved-program rows; on completion, provides a summary of successful updates plus a downloadable list of errors (e.g. 'Unique ID not found'); captures the uploader's Unique ID and upload timestamp in the audit log, distinguishing admin-on-behalf-of-EPP actions from EPP-user actions." ;
    sd:satisfiedBy epp:Seq_BulkUploadCandidateTrackingData, epp:Op_InitiateBulkUpload, epp:Op_CompleteBulkUpload, epp:Op_BulkCreateEnrollments, epp:BulkUploadCompletedEvent, epp:Perm_EnrollmentBulkUpload ;
    sd:notes "THIS IS THE STORY THAT RESOLVES the open question left in GAPS.md's FDD 29 entry ('Candidate Tracking and Recommendation (25)... unconfirmed whether epp:Seq_BulkUploadCandidateTrackingData actually covers what FDD 29's Dependencies section is pointing at'): CONFIRMED — epp:Seq_BulkUploadCandidateTrackingData's own error scenarios ('Unique ID not found in IAM > Skip row, include in error report'; 'Program not approved for EPP > Skip row, include in error report') and its Synapse-pipeline validate-then-partial-success-then-error-report flow match this story's acceptance criteria closely, feature for feature. Two minor, non-blocking gaps, neither large enough to warrant its own Annotation: (1) the modeled audit trail ('Capture audit trail with bulk upload job ID', plus 'uploadedBy' in the initiate payload) does not explicitly distinguish an admin acting on behalf of an EPP from the EPP user acting directly, which this story calls for; (2) HLS Use Case 34 ('System Admin downloads and extracts the submitted data') has no dedicated modeled operation — Wireframe25_AddendumCandidatesVerifiedAddStudent shows a download icon on the same screen as the Add Student upload trigger, a plausible fit for docs:Op_DownloadDocument against the staging container, but this is inferred, not confirmed by any caption or acceptance-criteria text." ;
    sd:definedIn epp:Fdd25CandidateTrackingDoc .
